# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Keeps `docker compose build` (dev image) and `docker build` (production
# multi-stage image) fast by preventing large/local-only artefacts from being
# sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# NOTE: The production Dockerfile is a multi-stage build. The build stage needs
# the Rust sources, Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, and any config it bakes in. The
# runtime stage copies only the compiled binary and config from the build
# stage. Anything mounted into the dev container at runtime is unaffected —
# `docker-compose.yml` bind-mounts the whole repo into /workspace, so these
# exclusions only apply to the image *build* step, not to the running container.
# =============================================================================

# Rust build artefacts — can be many GB; regenerated inside the container
target/
**/target/

# Git history and metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# GitHub / CI metadata
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Node / API layer (not needed inside the Rust image)
api/node_modules/
api/dist/
api/.env
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# Python / pre-commit caches
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Test snapshots and coverage artefacts (regenerated by cargo test)
**/test_snapshots/
**/lcov.info
**/coverage/

# Tests — not required to compile the production binary
tests/
**/tests/
benches/
**/benches/
examples/
**/examples/

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs / Markdown not required to compile the Rust image
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Monitoring stack (dev-only; not part of the production image)
monitoring/
**/monitoring/node_modules/

# Local env files and secrets — never bake these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Large local config that should not be baked into the image
config/local.toml

# Docker files themselves (not needed inside the build context)
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>
</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>
</｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>